cherrytree-docmodel (1.7.2+docmodel17-1) plucky; urgency=low

  * Password protect any subtree, encrypted inside the same document
  * Locked areas are hidden from the tree, from searches and from exports
  * Areas re-lock automatically after a configurable idle time, 5 minutes by default
  * Several independent password protected areas per document
  * Change the password or remove the protection, and lock every area with Ctrl+Shift+L
  * AES-256-CBC with HMAC-SHA256 and PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256, built on the bundled 7-Zip primitives, no new dependency
  * The encrypted content is authenticated before decryption, so a wrong password and a tampered document fail alike
  * Encrypted subtrees live in a new protected_area table and their nodes leave no rows of their own
  * Save As and Export to XML or MultiFile refuse while an area is locked, so protected content is never silently dropped
  * Tree menu and node context menu entries for password protection, with a Show Password option in the dialogs
  * Locked and unlocked areas are marked in the tree, and node properties shows the protection state
  * Search reports areas skipped because they are locked, and export warns before leaving them out
  * Bookmarks inside an area survive a lock, and undo entries for locked nodes are discarded
  * Fix new menu entries staying invisible for users with a menu layout saved by an earlier version

 -- Giuseppe Penone <giuspen@gmail.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 08:09:17 +0100

cherrytree-docmodel (1.7.2+docmodel16-1) plucky; urgency=low

  * Select tool for editing Bezier curve control points
  * Multi-select, scale tool, and apply properties to selection
  * Separate stroke and fill colors for drawing strokes
  * Arrow and DoubleArrow polygon shapes, closed freehand fill
  * Scrollbars for drawing canvases extending beyond visible page area
  * Font transform matrix for independent X/Y text scaling
  * Fix group scaling of rotated shapes
  * Fix drawing canvas undo/redo scrolling to bottom of page
  * Ensure group drawing operations undo/redo as a single step
  * Allow Ctrl+V to paste drawing canvases outside edit mode
  * Show node ID prefix on all drawing commands in undo/redo list

 -- Giuseppe Penone <giuspen@gmail.com>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 11:05:25 +0100

